From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fru-device: classify driver-owned addresses as normal scan skips

Keep I2C_SLAVE rather than forcing access to bound devices. Only EBUSY is
expected; retain actual selection errors and include errno in their logs.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD board policy]

--- a/src/fru_device/fru_device.cpp
+++ b/src/fru_device/fru_device.cpp
@@ -516,8 +516,20 @@
         // Set target address
         if (ioctl(file, I2C_SLAVE, ii) < 0)
         {
-            lg2::error("device at bus {BUS} address {ADDR} busy", "BUS", bus,
-                       "ADDR", ii);
+            const int error = errno;
+            if (error == EBUSY)
+            {
+                // I2C_SLAVE intentionally refuses addresses owned by a kernel
+                // driver. This is expected during an opportunistic FRU scan.
+                lg2::debug("Skipping driver-owned I2C address on bus {BUS}, "
+                           "address {ADDR}", "BUS", bus, "ADDR", ii);
+            }
+            else
+            {
+                lg2::error("Failed to select I2C address on bus {BUS}, "
+                           "address {ADDR}: errno {ERRNO}", "BUS", bus,
+                           "ADDR", ii, "ERRNO", error);
+            }
             continue;
         }
         // probe
